[
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"933054\">@Snir Broshi</span> and I have been working on mathlib4 PR #<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43034#issuecomment-5378290509\">43034</a>, which adds a computable greatest-prime-factor operation for natural numbers.  Should the new function be called <code>Nat.maxPrimeFac</code> or <code>Nat.maxPrimeFactor</code>? <code>Nat.maxFac</code> was understandably judged too broad, so I'd like to settle the spelling before renaming it again.</p>",
        "id": 618125511,
        "sender_full_name": "Bo Cowgill",
        "timestamp": 1787429362
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'd go for <code>Nat.maxPrimeFac</code> <strong>and</strong> rename the existing <code>Nat.minFac</code> to <code>Nat.minPrimeFac</code> to match, because 1 is a factor of every natural number</p>",
        "id": 618155150,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1787456568
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I prefer to spell out <code>Factor</code> based on this:</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"459227\">Violeta Hernández</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Rename.20.60.60.60LocPathConnectedSpace.60.60.60.3F/near/583134917\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't like abbreviations unless they're really obvious. I don't think Loc for Locally quite meets that threshold.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 618155607,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1787457154
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>well we already have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.minFac#doc\">docs#Nat.minFac</a></p>",
        "id": 618155652,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1787457218
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In my view <code>Nat.maxPrimeFac</code> really is really obvious</p>",
        "id": 618155692,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1787457259
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think we should prioritize consistency here, if we're gonna call this one with <code>factor</code> we should rename <code>Nat.minFac</code> to <code>Nat.minFactor</code> too</p>",
        "id": 618155706,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1787457279
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, although we could play the <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/antidiagonal.20vs.20antidiag/near/588753028\">\"diag\" vs \"diagonal\"</a> card here <span aria-label=\"see no evil\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f648\" role=\"img\" title=\"see no evil\">:see_no_evil:</span></p>",
        "id": 618155863,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1787457444
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>IMO <code>minPrimeFactor</code> &gt; <code>minPrimeFac</code> &gt; <code>minFactor</code> &gt; <code>minFac</code></p>",
        "id": 618155982,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1787457584
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, then <code>minPrimeFactor</code> and <code>maxPrimeFactor</code>!</p>",
        "id": 618156097,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1787457621
    }
]